years.\", \"line\": 3, \"span\": \"a journey that would take about 4,5 years\"},\n{\"text\": \"Voyager 2's encounter with Jupiter was optimized in part to ensure that future planetary flybys would be possible.\", \"line\": 3, \"span\": \"its encounter with Jupiter was optimized in part to ensure that future planetary flybys would be possible\"},\n{\"text\": \"The Uranus encounter's geometry was defined by the possibility of a future encounter with Neptune.\", \"line\": 3, \"span\": \"The Uranus encounter's geometry was also defined by the possibility of a future encounter with Neptune\"},\n{\"text\": \"Voyager 1 had only 6.4 days of close study during its flyby.\", \"line\": 3, \"span\": \"Voyager 1 had only 6.4 days of close study during its flyby\"},\n{\"text\": \"Voyager 2 was the first human-made object to fly past Uranus.\", \"line\": 5, \"span\": \"Voyager 2, the first human-made object to fly past Uranus\"},\n{\"text\": \"Voyager 2 began short-range observations of Uranus on Jan. 31, 1987.\", \"line\": 5, \"span\": \"began short-range observations of the planet on Jan. 31, 1987\"},\n{\"text\": \"Signals took approximately 2,5 hours to reach Earth at the time Voyager 2 began short-range observations of Uranus.\", \"line\": 5, \"span\": \"when signals took approximately 2,5 hours to reach Earth\"},\n{\"text\": \"Light conditions at Uranus were five-hundred times less than terrestrial conditions.\", \"line\": 5, \"span\": \"Light conditions were five-hundred times less than terrestrial conditions\"},\n{\"text\": \"Closest approach to Uranus took place at 17:59 ED Jan. 24, 1986.\", \"line\": 5, \"span\": \"Closest approach to Uranus took place at 17:59 ED Jan. 24, 1986\"},\n{\"text\": \"Closest approach to Uranus occurred at a range of about 81,500 kilometers (50,640 miles).\", \"line\": 5, \"span\": \"at a range of about 81,500 kilometers (50,640 miles)\"},\n{\"text\": \"During its flyby, Voyager 2 discovered 10 new moons.\", \"line\": 7, \"span\": \"Voyager 2 discovered 10 new moons\"},\n{\"text\": \"The 10 new moons discovered were given such names as Puck, Portia, Juliet, Cressida, Rosalind, Belinda, Desdemona, Cordelia, Ophelia, and Bianca.\", \"line\": 7, \"span\": \"given such names as Puck, Portia, Juliet, Cressida, Rosalind, Belinda, Desdemona, Cordelia, Ophelia, and Bianca\"},\n{\"text\": \"The names given to the moons are allusions to Shakespeare.\", \"line\": 7, \"span\": \"obvious allusions to Shakespeare\"},\n{\"text\": \"The Shakespeare naming tradition for the moons was begun in 1787.\", \"line\": 7, \"span\": \"continuing a naming tradition begun in 1787\"},\n{\"text\": \"During its flyby, Voyager 2 discovered two new rings in addition to the nine previously known rings.\", \"line\": 7, \"span\": \"two new rings in addition to the nine previously known rings\"},\n{\"text\": \"During its flyby, Voyager 2 discovered a magnetic field tilted at 59 degrees off-axis and off-center.\", \"line\": 7, \"span\": \"a magnetic field tilted at 59 degrees off-axis and off-center\"},\n{\"text\": \"The spacecraft found wind speeds in Uranus' atmosphere as high as 450 km/h (450,000 meters per hour).\", \"line\": 9, \"span\": \"The spacecraft found wind speeds in Uranus' atmosphere as high as 450 km/h (450,000 meters per hour)\"},\n{\"text\": \"The spacecraft found evidence of a boiling lake of water some 559 miles (900 kilometers) below the top cloud surface.\", \"line\": 9, \"span\": \"found evidence of a boiling lake of water some 559 miles (900 kilometers) below the top cloud surface\"},\n{\"text\": \"Uranus' rings were found to be extremely variable in thickness and transparency.\", \"line\": 9, \"span\": \"Its rings were found to be extremely variable in thickness and transparency\"},\n{\"text\": \"Voyager 2 returned photos of Miranda, Oberon, Ariel, Umbriel, and Titania.\", \"line\": 11, \"span\": \"Voyager 2 also returned spectacular photos of Miranda, Oberon, Ariel, Umbriel, and Titania\"},\n{\"text\": \"Miranda, Oberon, Ariel, Umbriel, and Titania are five of Uranus' smaller moons.\", \"line\": 11, \"span\": \"five of Uranus' smaller moons\"},\n{\"text\": \"Voyager 2 flew by Miranda at a range of only 17.560 miles (28.260 kilometers).\", \"line\": 11, \"span\": \"In flying by Miranda at a range of only 17.560 miles (28.260 kilometers)\"},\n{\"text\": \"The flyby of Miranda was the closest Voyager 2 came to any object so far in its nearly decade-long travels.\", \"line\": 11, \"span\": \"the spacecraft came closest to any object so far in its nearly decade-long travels\"},\n{\"text\": \"Images of Miranda showed a surface that was a mishmash of peculiar features.\", \"line\": 11, \"span\": \"Images of the moon showed a strange object whose surface was a mishmash of peculiar features that seemed to have no rhyme or reason\"},\n{\"text\": \"Uranus itself appeared generally featureless.\", \"line\": 11, \"span\": \"Uranus itself appeared generally featureless\"},\n{\"text\": \"The news of the Uranus encounter was interrupted the same day by the Challenger accident.\", \"line\": 13, \"span\": \"The spectacular news of the Uranus encounter was interrupted the same day by the tragic Challenger accident\"},\n{\"text\": \"The Challenger accident killed seven astronauts during their space shuttle launch.\", \"line\": 13, \"span\": \"that killed seven astronauts during their space shuttle launch\"},\n{\"text\": \"The Challenger accident occurred on Jan. 28, 1986.\", \"line\": 13, \"span\": \"space shuttle launch Jan. 28, 1986\"}\n]}","ttft_ms":15625,"type":"result","duration_ms":15663,"uuid":"91694a24-1e4d-4328-8bad-ac2a50a7247b","ttft_stream_ms":1515,"time_to_request_ms":114,"first_content_frame_ms":1515,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
